## Tool

```bash
python tools/h5m/h5m.py summary  G:/__H5__/H5Xdev/Maps/H5X_Stadium.h5m
python tools/h5m/h5m.py terrain  G:/__H5__/H5Xdev/Maps/H5X_Stadium.h5m
python tools/h5m/h5m.py regions  G:/__H5__/H5Xdev/Maps/H5X_Stadium.h5m out/stadium 0
```

`regions` writes `<out>.png` (6 px per tile, y up; dark = blocked, blue = water / rim, red = monster guard zones, orange = garrisons, white = visit tiles, other colours = regions) and `<out>.txt` (each region with its bounding box and the objects visited from it, then every monster / garrison with the regions it separates). Regions are 8-connected walkable tiles outside guard zones. Needs `numpy` and `Pillow`.
